Z||000000||Fierowrecker||09-11-2001||10:28 PM||||I live out in the country, about 20 miles from a major airport...<BR>Normally, I see dozens of aircraft strobe lights in the sky, but tonight, there isn't a single strobe flashing...<BR>It is very unsettling to realize one of our major forms of transportation has been stopped completely...<BR>I understand why, but it still hits hard how a few terrorists can paralize a nation built on freedom...<BR>And I am also discusted by gas station owners jacking up the price of gas in such a time, when mothers, fathers, brothers and sisters need to go home after being stranded far from home, and the only way open is by ground, unless the skies are open by noon tomorrow as reported in the news...<BR>crash...||||reg||4
Z||000001||Sleeper||09-11-2001||10:41 PM||||i know what you mean, i live about 10 miles south of LAX. usually if i look east at night i can see a line on jets coming in but not tonight. <BR>speaking of LAX i hear its a skeleton, nobody going in and nobody going out, completely dead.||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||09-11-2001||10:54 PM||||Live about 10 miles from Selfridge Air Force Base east of Detroit, haven't heard this much "Afterburner" traffic since Viet Nam, the boys must be busy!!! Other than that I don't think there's ever been a quieter night in my lifetime!!! Very few cars on the road to.||||reg||1
Z||000003||72vinman||09-11-2001||11:03 PM||||I know what you mean guys. I live 10 minutes away from Canada'a largest airport. My house is directly in line with one of the runways. Usually planes are landing every 2 minutes. Except for tonight....<BR>The only air traffic in Canada today was for US flights that needed to land. Other than that all airports were closed.<BR>Very Very quiet night||||reg||1
Z||000004||gt boy||09-11-2001||11:08 PM||||even though i live in ontario canada, it is also very quiet around toronto international airport too...since our govmt is going along with grounding all flights...i work all around the airport and i saw only 3 planes coming in in 1 1/2 hours.(traffic is 84 planes/hour in and out)<P>my condolences to all my american friends.  i could not believe what i was hearing and seeing on CNN..it just brought tears to my eyes.<P>all the moms and dads not coming home tonight tears me apart.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000005||JetroGT||09-12-2001||08:18 AM||||I work during the night in Fort Worth, relatively near DFW international. Usually there's about 5 or 6 plains visible at any given time, but tonight only the stars were out. Going back into work was just as strange. Every bench has a computer hooked to a network. And on every computer CNN was plastered to the screans as people watched this horrable day for 12 hours. I was up yesterday at 9:30 when I was woken up by a friend in Kenosha Wisconsin. She told me to "Get up and turn on the news! Planes have crashed into the twin towers!" I turned on the TV to see just one tower that resembled a lit cigerett. I sat and watched it untill noon. I went back to sleep. I had a nightmare about Columbia attacking America and America fighting back. Then at 6pm I went to work where the news just kept coming all night. This is just unreal.||||reg||1
